       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.** That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose. The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and it is usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nMy guess is that 2,550 mg was meant as the total daily dose. Which of these did you intend?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day total\n- **Another dose or frequency**, such as 500 mg twice daily or 1,000 mg twice daily\n- **2,550 mg three times daily as written.** If so, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note that you verified the dose.\n\nOnce you pick one, I'll enter it right away."
      }
